Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: png.c
Line: 495
Function: png_free_data
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: Indexes info_ptr->text[num] without validating that 'num' is within bounds (and also allows negative values other than -1). If 'num' is out of range, this performs an out-of-bounds access: first reads an out-of-bounds pointer value to free, then writes to info_ptr->text[num].key = NULL, corrupting heap memory. This can be triggered by calling png_free_data(..., PNG_FREE_TEXT, num) with an invalid 'num'.

